  {
   "k": "1i0c0if",
   "en": "Railway artillery movement on land is limited to only on railway lines. Railway artillery can be transported over water by first manually moving it to a railway-connected port before embarking it to another port. Embarked railway artillery ignores ⟦0⟧, so care must be taken to move them in ways where they avoid sea zones that the player wishes them to avoid.",
